Is there anybody here who is using the savage X driver to run a video card 
(not a laptop) that has TV-out capability (that is, output to an NTSC 
composite television screen)?

The site for the driver (http://www.probo.com/timr/savage40.html) says it 
supports TV-out, but with the actual Savage card I have (a Savage 2000), I 
can't seem to find the trick to make it work. Nor can I find any discussion 
anywhere of what the problem might be ... everything I find when I search 
is specific to Savage chipsets in laptops.

If anyone a working XF86Config-4 file for this setup, I'd appreciate seeing 
it. Naturally, I can provide more details if anyone wants them, but the 
basic description of the X-on-TV display I get, no matter what I try, is "a 
mess".


